{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>לרצנכם תזבחו.</b> At the outset of your slaughter, take heed that it be for your acceptance — and what is the acceptance?" "<b>ביום ההוא יאכל.</b> It comes only to warn that the slaughter be on that condition — do not slaughter it on condition to eat it tomorrow, for if you have in it a disqualifying intent, it will not be for your acceptance. Another interpretation: <b>לרצנכם</b> — בְּדַעְתְּכֶם [with your knowledge]; from here [we learn] concerning one who acts unawares, who invalidates the slaughter of consecrated offerings. And even though He specified for those eaten [over] two days, He returned and specified for those eaten [for] one day — that their slaughter be on condition to eat them in their time."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:50.009847649Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}